{"event":"step_update","step_update":{"conversation_id":"93523d3b-46df-4ef0-8404-ed18864cbbdd","step_index":6,"state":"DONE","step_type":"tool","tool_name":"run_command","duration_seconds":0.031801071,"tool_info":{"name":"run_command","parameters":{"CommandLine":"git show 2426346"},"output":"commit 2426346b951604a190a367aa95843859d92b0a6d (HEAD -\u003e dispatch/9, master)\r\nAuthor: FLYBYME \u003cmangoraft@gmail.com\u003e\r\nDate:   Sun Sep 6 20:45:41 2026 -0400\r\n\r\n    Queue 9: F5, make a kernel mismatch fatal at compose time\r\n\r\ndiff --git a/agent-runs/prompts/9-kernel-mismatch.prompt.txt b/agent-runs/prompts/9-kernel-mismatch.prompt.txt\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000..d5a4ee5\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/agent-runs/prompts/9-kernel-mismatch.prompt.txt\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,96 @@\r\n+Code lives in:  FLYBYME/mesh-serve — this worktree. All commits go here.\r\n+\r\n+================================================================================\r\n+THE TASK\r\n+================================================================================\r\n+\r\n+**F5 — `partVersion.kernel` is stored and never read.** Rated **S**. Make a\r\n+kernel mismatch a fatal composition problem.\r\n+\r\n+`publish-cli` writes the range a part was built against, with the comment *\"the\r\n+only thing standing between a stale part and a browser\"*. `build_start` forwards\r\n+it. **Nothing reads it.** `checkComposition` checks missing required parts, unmet\r\n+contracts and unused grants, and has **no kernel case at all**.\r\n+\r\n+Add a `kernel_mismatch` problem, **fatal** — the same class as a missing required\r\n+part, not a warning like an unused grant.\r\n+\r\n+================================================================================\r\n+IT IS NOT THEORETICAL, AND HERE IS THE MEASUREMENT\r\n+================================================================================\r\n+\r\n+The roadmap entry cites one historical violation. Measured against the live\r\n+platform on 2026-09-06, before that day's rebuild, **five of six live sites were\r\n+serving parts outside their declared range**:\r\n+\r\n+| site | kernel served | parts declaring |\r\n+| --- | --- | --- |\r\n+| `demos.localhost` | 0.11.4 | `theme` `clock` `notes` `calc` — all `^0.6` |\r\n+| `todo.localhost` | 0.11.4 | `todo` `^0.6` |\r\n+| `demo.localhost` · `localhost` · `127.0.0.1` | 0.11.4 | `auth@0.2.0` `^0.6` |\r\n+| `console.localhost` | 0.11.4 | `chrome` `catalog` `releases` `^0.11` ✓ |\r\n+\r\n+`^0.6` is `\u003e=0.6.0 \u003c0.7.0`. Every one of those compositions should have been\r\n+refused and none was.\r\n+\r\n+**And when the range was finally enforced by hand**, bumping `mesh-demos` from\r\n+`^0.6` to `^0.13` immediately failed to compile: `workbench` had narrowed the\r\n+window mode to `'windowed' | 'tiled'` in four places and the kernel had gained\r\n+`'single'`. That is a real incompatibility this check would have surfaced at\r\n+compose time instead of leaving it to a browser.\r\n+\r\n+================================================================================\r\n+WHERE IT GOES\r\n+================================================================================\r\n+\r\n+    src/cdn/methods/release.ts       checkComposition — the distinctions are the\r\n+                                     point: a required part absent **refuses**,\r\n+                                     an optional one **reports**, an unmet\r\n+                                     contract **refuses**, an unused grant\r\n+                                     **reports**. A kernel mismatch refuses.\r\n+    src/catalog/schema/part.ts       partVersion.kernel, and its comment\r\n+    src/cdn/tools/compose.ts         the caller\r\n+    spec/unread.md §1                the `partVersion.kernel` row, which this\r\n+                                     closes — update it to say what happened,\r\n+                                     the way the `release.exposure` row was\r\n+                                     updated by D4\r\n+\r\n+**A kernel artifact has no kernel requirement of its own** — the one thing that\r\n+has no kernel. `DeclarationSchema.kernel` is `.optional()` for exactly that\r\n+reason. An absent range is not a mismatch.\r\n+\r\n+**Decide what an absent range means for a *part*, and say why.** Versions\r\n+published before the field existed have none. Refusing them breaks every existing\r\n+release; accepting them silently is how the field became decorative in the first\r\n+place. There is a third option — accept, and report it as a non-fatal problem —\r\n+and it may be the right one. Argue it rather than picking quietly.\r\n+\r\n+================================================================================\r\n+WHAT GOOD LOOKS LIKE\r\n+================================================================================\r\n+\r\n+- **A test composing kernel 0.13 with a part declaring `^0.6`, refused, naming\r\n+  both the part and the range.** That is the whole item.\r\n+- A test that a kernel artifact's own absent requirement is not a mismatch.\r\n+- A test for whatever you decide an absent range means on a part.\r\n+- A test that a satisfied range composes cleanly — the six live sites are all in\r\n+  range as of the rebuild, so a false positive here breaks production.\r\n+- Every existing test passing. `npm run typecheck` clean, **zero casts**.\r\n+- Tick F5 in `spec/roadmap.md`; update the `partVersion.kernel` row in\r\n+  `spec/unread.md` §1.\r\n+\r\n+**Run every command in the foreground. Commit as you go.**\r\n+\r\n+================================================================================\r\n+YOUR REPORT\r\n+================================================================================\r\n+\r\n+`agent-runs/reports/9-kernel-mismatch.md`\r\n+\r\n+- what an absent range means on a part, and the argument\r\n+- **whether any release currently in the database would now be refused.** The\r\n+  platform was rebuilt clean earlier today so the answer should be none — if it\r\n+  is not none, that is the finding and it matters more than the code.\r\n+- whether `checkComposition`'s four problem kinds are still the right set, now\r\n+  that there are five\r\n+- anything for `spec/unread.md`\r\n"}}}
